course: dictionary
lesson: 15730
title: One word, three subjects
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to more than one subject, and each subject uses them in its own way. Transformation is one of these words. In maths it is about moving or changing a shape. In science it is about changing from one form to another. In stories it is about a character who changes.
explain: Read the words around it to find out which meaning is used. «The triangle slid three squares to the right, a transformation on the grid.» The words grid and slid are clues: this is maths. «The tadpole's transformation into a frog took eight weeks.» Tadpole, frog and weeks are clues: this is science.
explain: «The grumpy king's transformation made him kind to everyone.» Here the clue is the change in how the king behaves, so this is a story. Ask yourself what kind of text you are reading, then choose the meaning that fits.
fact: Transformation means a big change in how someone or something looks, works or behaves.
fact: In maths, a transformation moves or changes a shape: a translation (slide), reflection (flip), rotation (turn) or enlargement.
fact: In maths, the new shape after a transformation is called the image.
fact: In science, a transformation is a change from one form to another, like a caterpillar becoming a butterfly.
fact: Two useful phrases are «a complete transformation» (a total change) and «undergo a transformation» (go through a change).
exercise: In maths, what is a slide of a shape on a grid called? | Reflection | *Translation | Rotation | Enlargement
exercise: «The tadpole's transformation into a frog took eight weeks.» Which subject does this sentence come from? | History | *Science | Music | Maths
exercise: «After the lesson, Sam had a complete transformation in how he spoke to others.» What does transformation mean here? | A short pause before speaking | *A big change in how Sam behaves | A loud noise in the hall | A flip of Sam's picture on a grid
test: In maths, what do we call the new shape after a transformation? | *Image | Border | Outline | Pattern
test: «The prince was once a frog, and his transformation surprised everyone.» What does transformation mean in this sentence? | *A big change, from a frog into a prince | A tidy-up of the castle | A long walk to the palace | A kind of drink
exam: Which of these is a turn of a shape on a grid? | *Rotation | Translation | Enlargement | Reflection
